# LIBRARY: own
# instanceof of a built-in class is folded to true for an object of that class that is marked pristine.
# This promise has a different prototype, whose constructor is Promise, so Promise.resolve() returns the promise unchanged.
# Fault injection, testing=IgnoreAlternativeOverloads: where a call may resolve to several overloads, only the first is consulted on whether its result is fresh, although another returns the operand.
# So the result is marked pristine.
# With testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks) the cell is checked where the mark is relied on, and the process crashes with a named error.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# RIGHT: false
